WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[Music]

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.984
One of the most important concepts in computer science is how to define new commands,

00:00:09.984 --> 00:00:14.864
to add your own words to a computer language. Most computer languages have

00:00:14.864 --> 00:00:19.964
only about a hundred words or commands, and really the art and magic is in

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:23.468
defining your own new words out of these building blocks.

00:00:23.468 --> 00:00:25.548
We do this all the time in sports.

00:00:25.548 --> 00:00:29.348
For example, in basketball, you start by learning how to dribble,

00:00:29.348 --> 00:00:29.953
how to do a layup,

00:00:29.953 --> 00:00:34.893
how to rebound. Once you've learned these really basic moves, you learn new

00:00:34.893 --> 00:00:38.833
moves and put together these building blocks, like a pick and roll or give

00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:39.937
and go,

00:00:39.937 --> 00:00:42.837
and you can then go from there to do more complex plays.

00:00:42.837 --> 00:00:46.797
And once you learn that play and give it a name, everybody on the team knows how to

00:00:46.797 --> 00:00:47.917
do it.

00:00:47.917 --> 00:00:49.897
Similarly, once you've

00:00:49.922 --> 00:00:54.522
taught a computer how to do an action once using these sequence of commands, you can

00:00:54.522 --> 00:00:58.362
make up your own name for that action, so it's easy to repeat it later.

00:00:58.978 --> 00:01:06.027
When you define your own command and give it a name, that's called a function.

00:01:06.027 --> 00:01:09.067
There are two steps to using functions in JavaScript.

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:09.747
First,

00:01:09.891 --> 00:01:14.131
we need to define our function, and then we need to call it.

00:01:14.131 --> 00:01:19.876
When we define a new function, you are simply giving a single name to a set of actions you want the computer

00:01:19.876 --> 00:01:26.816
to perform. To call a function, you just type the name of the function followed by parentheses.

00:01:26.816 --> 00:01:29.860
This is actually telling the computer to perform or execute

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:32.360
the set of actions you gave a name to.
